# Image findings with no fixed Debian package, accepted 2026-11-07 (security
# triage). Each is a library deploy/pushleft/Dockerfile cannot drop, with why
# the CVE is out of reach. Untrusted files reach native code only through
# Disk::Thumbnailer (vips with VIPS_BLOCK_UNTRUSTED, pdftoppm, and ffmpeg held to
# its demuxer and decoder lists), pdftotext (AttachmentTextExtractor) and rspamd.
# Never list a CVE that has a fix: rebuild instead (APT_UPGRADE_AT).

# OpenEXR, cfitsio, matio, ImageMagick: hard dependencies of Debian's
# libvips42t64, reached only through vips's openexrload, fitsload, matload and
# magickload, all untrusted loaders the thumbnailer blocks.
CVE-2025-12495
CVE-2025-12839
CVE-2025-12840
CVE-2025-64181
CVE-2026-27622
CVE-2026-34379
CVE-2026-34543
CVE-2026-34544
CVE-2026-34545
CVE-2026-34588
CVE-2026-40244
CVE-2026-40250
CVE-2026-41142
CVE-2026-42216
CVE-2026-42217
CVE-2026-59184
CVE-2026-59186
CVE-2026-59187
CVE-2026-59189
CVE-2026-59981
CVE-2026-59982
CVE-2026-115504
CVE-2025-2338
CVE-2026-119123

# FFmpeg: NVDEC needs an NVIDIA GPU (none); the VobSub demuxer and the RASC
# decoder are off the thumbnailer's -format_whitelist and -codec_whitelist; the
# S/PDIF muxer is never used (output is one PNG frame).
CVE-2026-64832
CVE-2026-64830
CVE-2026-58049
CVE-2026-64833

# libxml2 use-after-free: Nokogiri ships its own libxml2; the system one is
# reached by untrusted input only through librsvg and ImageMagick (blocked vips
# loaders) and FFmpeg's DASH demuxer (not on the format list).
CVE-2026-6653

# libtiff: process_command_opts is in the tiff command-line tools, not the
# library; the SamplesPerPixel DoS ends in the thumbnailer's killed-after-60s
# child process.
CVE-2026-52490
CVE-2026-36849

# libXi (libsdl2, pulled by ffmpeg's libavdevice) talks to an X server: none.
CVE-2026-109089
CVE-2026-109090
# libsndfile ima_reader (libpulse, pulled by libavdevice): no sound I/O here.
CVE-2026-37555
# cJSON (librist, pulled by libavformat): the RIST protocol is never opened.
CVE-2026-29036
CVE-2026-16554
# GnuPG tpm2daemon (pulled by poppler's gpgme): never started, no TPM.
CVE-2026-24882
# curl SFTP/SCP host check: nothing here fetches sftp:// or scp:// URLs.
CVE-2026-12064
# expat (fontconfig, vips, mesa): reads the image's own config files; vips's
# XML is only in .v files, whose loader is blocked.
CVE-2026-115506
CVE-2026-113351
CVE-2026-118370
CVE-2026-117610
# SQLite FTS5 and session changesets: rspamd's sqlite files are its own; no
# FTS5 index or changeset from outside is read.
CVE-2026-119374
CVE-2026-119379
CVE-2026-119373
# Local-only: systemd-homed (not running in a container), libacl symlink
# traversal (no setuid ACL tools), ncurses (no terminal input from users).
CVE-2026-16742
CVE-2026-54369
CVE-2025-69720

# Found by a newer Trivy DB on the 2026-11-07 rebuild, not yet in Pushleft's scan.
# FFmpeg: RTP/ASF, CAF, WTV, DASH and MPEG-PS are off -format_whitelist, RIST
# is never opened, ADX/AAX, PGS, CFHD, Dirac and PNG decoders are off
# -codec_whitelist, hqdn3d is a filter we never run, HEVC muxing never happens.
CVE-2026-64834
CVE-2026-64835
